      "content": "Answer the following question with a single MySQL SQL query against the current database. Explore the semantic network and verify with mysql_query as needed. The SELECT list must contain exactly the columns the question asks for, in the asked order. When the final SQL is verified, call the submit_SQL tool with it.\n\nThe following hints are provided to help you write the SQL:\n\n## Gold Tables\n- TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED\n- SIS_DEPARTMENT\n- SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL\n- ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER\n\n## Column Mapping\n- department: SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME, TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_NAME\n- average enrollment: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\n- enrollment variance: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\n- subjects offered: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_ID\n- enrolled students: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\n- degree-granting courses: SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING\n- departments: SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME, SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE\n- Political Science: SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE\n- Chemistry: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_NAME\n- Biology: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_NAME\n- academic year: ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL.ACADEMIC_YEAR\n- subject count: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_ID\n- minimum term start date: ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL.TERM_START_DATE\n\n## Join Keys\n- SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE <-> TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_CODE\n- SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.DEPARTMENT <-> SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL.TERM_CODE <-> TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL.TERM_CODE <-> ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER.TERM_CODE\n\n## Question\nFor each department, what is the average and variance of the number of enrolled students in subjects offered by that department (considering only subjects with more than 0 enrolled students, degree-granting courses, and excluding departments that are 'Political Science' (Course 17)), and for Chemistry and Biology departments and each academic year where the number of enrolled students in a subject is greater than 0, what is the count of subjects and the minimum start date of the term? Present the department name, average enrollment, enrollment variance, academic year, subject count, and minimum term start date in that order. Do not return any rounded answers."
