      "content": "The database connection remains down (persistent authentication error across many retries). I have gathered comprehensive semantic evidence, so let me consolidate the analysis and produce the final report and SQL.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Entity Semantics\n\n**Tables (Phase 1 survivors, all investigated via `semantic_get`):**\n\n- **TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED** — Textbook Information Program subject offering table; one row per subject per term in the textbook program. Key columns: `SUBJECT_ID`, `TERM_CODE`, `OFFER_DEPT_CODE` (joins to SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE), `OFFER_DEPT_NAME` (e.g. 'Chemistry', 'Biology'), `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS` (\"Number of students enrolled in the subject; used for enrollment-based rankings and window statistics\").\n- **SIS_DEPARTMENT** — Department dimension; one row per academic department. Key columns: `DEPARTMENT_CODE`, `DEPARTMENT_NAME`, `IS_DEGREE_GRANTING`, `SCHOOL_NAME`.\n- **SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION** — Catalog course descriptions; one row per course description. Key columns: `COURSE`, `DEPARTMENT` (joins to SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE), `IS_DEGREE_GRANTING` (\"'Y'/'N' flag whether the course counts toward a degree\"), `COURSE_LEVEL`.\n- **ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL** — Extended term dimension (superset of ACADEMIC_TERMS). Key columns: `TERM_CODE`, `ACADEMIC_YEAR`, `TERM_START_DATE`, `ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC`.\n- **ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER** — Exactly three rows identifying SIS current/previous/upcoming terms; key columns `TERM_PARAMETER`, `TERM_INDICATOR`, `TERM_CODE` (joins to term tables' TERM_CODE).\n- **ACADEMIC_TERMS** — Status-tracked term subset (has IS_REGULAR_TERM, TERM_STATUS, ADD/DROP_DATE which ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL lacks). Investigated as a similar entity; not in the gold-table list.\n\n**Metrics investigated (precedents):** dw_1165, dw_1350, dw_2958, dw_4405, dw_1689, dw_4229, dw_3224, dw_4515, dw_5095, dw_3237, dw_1474, dw_4231.\n\n**Concepts:** concept_subject_offering_facts, concept_department_dimension, concept_academic_term_dimension, concept_course_material_programs. **Column concepts:** column_concept_enrollment_measures, column_concept_department_name, column_concept_subject_id, column_concept_term_code, column_concept_year_columns.\n\n### 2. Lineage & Relationships\n\n- Graph traversal on TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED confirmed outgoing joins to **SIS_DEPARTMENT** (OFFER_DEPT_CODE = DEPARTMENT_CODE), **ACADEMIC_TERMS**, **ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL**, **ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER** (via TERM_CODE), and incoming joins from TIP_DETAIL, LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED; concept memberships in concept_subject_offering_facts and concept_course_material_programs.\n- SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION joins SIS_DEPARTMENT via `DEPARTMENT = DEPARTMENT_CODE` (documented in its column defs and used in dw_1165's SQL).\n- ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER metrics (17 via `metrics_by_table`) include dw_4231 and dw_3224, both chaining `TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED → ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL → ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER` on TERM_CODE — exactly the join keys given in the hints.\n\n### 3. Similar-Entity Differences\n\n**3a. Dimension matrix (enrollment source candidates):**\n\n| Candidate | Granularity | Enrollment column | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED | one row per subject per term (textbook program scope) | NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS | column def: \"used for enrollment-based rankings and window statistics\" |\n| SUBJECT_OFFERED | one row per **section** | NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS | table desc (section-level → fan-out risk for subject stats) |\n| SUBJECT_SUMMARY / SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY | subject-level registrar summaries | SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER / NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS | column_concept_enrollment_measures: two families |\n\n**3b. Task-Requirement Fitness:**\n- Required measure `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS` for \"average enrollment\"/\"enrollment variance\": hint maps both to **TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS** → SUPPORTED only on TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED (per hints); SUBJECT_OFFERED is section-grain (VIOLATES subject-level semantics per hints).\n- \"degree-granting courses\" → hint maps to **SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING** (course-level flag), not SIS_DEPARTMENT.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING → SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION SUPPORTED.\n- \"academic year\" / \"minimum term start date\" → hints map to **ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL.ACADEMIC_YEAR / TERM_START_DATE**; ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL is the superset (covers terms ACADEMIC_TERMS may lack) → SUPPORTED.\n- ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER is a gold table with join key `ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL.TERM_CODE ↔ ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER.TERM_CODE` → must appear in the term join chain (as in dw_4231/dw_3224 precedents).\n\n**3c. Wording-to-Field Anchoring:**\n- \"excluding departments that are 'Political Science' (Course 17)\" → hint maps Political Science to **SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE** → `sd.DEPARTMENT_CODE <> '17'` (dw_1474 precedent uses the same Course-17 exclusion).\n- \"Chemistry and Biology departments\" → hint maps both to **TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_NAME** → `OFFER_DEPT_NAME IN ('Chemistry','Biology')` (dw_1165 precedent uses exactly this predicate on the same column).\n- \"more than 0 enrolled students\" → `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS > 0` (dw_4229/dw_4405 precedents use `> 0` / `> 5` on this column).\n- \"count of subjects\" (not \"unique subjects\") → `COUNT(SUBJECT_ID)`; precedents saying \"number of **unique** subjects\" (dw_4405, dw_4515) use COUNT(DISTINCT), while \"number of subjects offered\" (dw_3237) uses a plain COUNT — the wording here lacks \"unique\", anchoring to plain COUNT.\n- \"department name\" output → canonical `SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME` (Part 1 grouping key per hint \"departments: DEPARTMENT_NAME, DEPARTMENT_CODE\").\n\n**3d. Precedent Usage Evidence:**\n- AVG/VARIANCE of TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS per department with SIS_DEPARTMENT join: 3 precedents (dw_1165, dw_1350, dw_1689) — all use `VARIANCE()` and join `tso.OFFER_DEPT_CODE = sd.DEPARTMENT_CODE`; dw_1165 additionally joins SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION on `sd.DEPARTMENT_CODE = scd.DEPARTMENT` and groups by `sd.DEPARTMENT_NAME, sd.DEPARTMENT_CODE`.\n- Two-part \"for each X … and for Chemistry-related scope …\" questions combined via **CROSS JOIN**: 2 precedents (dw_1689 — school stats × Chemistry subject rows; dw_4405 — activity ranks × dept-year stats).\n- `TIP → ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL → ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER` TERM_CODE chain: 2 precedents (dw_4231, dw_3224).\n\n### 4. Business Usage\n\n- TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED is the standard source for textbook-program enrollment statistics per department (dw_1165, dw_1350, dw_1689, dw_4229, dw_4405 all consume NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS for AVG/VARIANCE/range per department).\n- SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION is used as a course-level filter dimension joined at department level (dw_1165: `COURSE_LEVEL='G'`; here `IS_DEGREE_GRANTING='Y'`). Note the department-level join fans out TIP rows uniformly per department; AVG and VARIANCE (population) are invariant under uniform duplication, so statistics are unaffected.\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL + ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER serve term enrichment (academic year, start date) and relative-term resolution.\n\n### 5. Coverage Checklist\n\n- TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED, SIS_DEPARTMENT, SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION, ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL, ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER, ACADEMIC_TERMS — `semantic_get` ✓, graph neighbors on TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED ✓, metrics_by_table on ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER ✓.\n- Metrics dw_1165, dw_1350, dw_2958, dw_4405, dw_3224, dw_4515, dw_5095, dw_3237, dw_1474, dw_4231, dw_1689, dw_4229 — `semantic_get` (full SQL) ✓.\n- Concepts/column-concepts (subject_offering_facts, department_dimension, academic_term_dimension, course_material_programs; enrollment_measures, department_name, subject_id, term_code, year_columns) — retrieved via search descriptions and graph ✓.\n- **mysql_query verification was impossible**: every attempt (10+ retries over the session) failed with `1045 Access denied for user 'root'@'localhost'` — an infrastructure credential error, not a SQL error. The SQL below is therefore validated against documented column definitions and metric-SQL precedents only.\n\n### 6. Recommendation\n\n**6a. Tables/columns:**\n- Part 1 (per department): TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED (`NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS` measure, `OFFER_DEPT_CODE` join key) ⋈ SIS_DEPARTMENT (`DEPARTMENT_NAME` output/group key, `DEPARTMENT_CODE <> '17'` exclusion) ⋈ SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION (`IS_DEGREE_GRANTING='Y'`, joined `DEPARTMENT = DEPARTMENT_CODE`); filter `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS > 0`; `AVG()` + `VARIANCE()`.\n- Part 2 (Chemistry/Biology per academic year): TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED (`OFFER_DEPT_NAME IN ('Chemistry','Biology')`, `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS > 0`, `COUNT(SUBJECT_ID)`) ⋈ ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL (`ACADEMIC_YEAR`, `MIN(TERM_START_DATE)`) ⋈ ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER (gold-table join on TERM_CODE, precedent dw_4231/dw_3224).\n- Combination: CROSS JOIN (precedent dw_1689/dw_4405 for this exact two-part question shape; the elaborate Part-1 filters — degree-granting, Course-17 exclusion — only affect the output if all departments survive, which a cross join guarantees; an inner join on department would render those filters inert and contradict \"For each department\").\n\n**6b. SQL approach:** two CTEs aggregated at their respective granularities (department; academic year), cross-joined, SELECT list exactly: department name, average enrollment, enrollment variance, academic year, subject count, minimum term start date. No rounding. Uniform fan-out from SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION does not distort AVG/VARIANCE (population variance invariant under row duplication).\n\n**6c. Three-perspective reasons:**\n- **Data**: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED is subject-grain (no section fan-out); NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS physically exists per its column def; ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL covers all terms (superset); ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER has exactly 3 rows with unique TERM_CODEs → its join filters without fanning out.\n- **Semantic network**: all four join keys are exactly the documented/hinted edges; graph confirms TIP→SIS_DEPARTMENT, TIP→ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL→ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER; column concepts anchor OFFER_DEPT_NAME for Chemistry/Biology and DEPARTMENT_NAME for the output.\n- **Business**: dw_1165/dw_1350/dw_1689 establish the AVG/VARIANCE-on-TIP-enrollment pattern with the same joins and filters; dw_1689/dw_4405 establish the CROSS JOIN composition for \"for each X … and for Chemistry scope …\" questions.\n\n**6d. Alternatives:** An inner join on department (restricting output to Chemistry/Biology) was considered and rejected because it would make the question's Political-Science exclusion and degree-granting filter unobservable in the output, contradicting the \"For each department\" wording; COUNT(DISTINCT SUBJECT_ID) was rejected because the question says \"count of subjects\", while distinct-count precedents (dw_4405/dw_4515) always say \"unique subjects\".\n\nFinal SQL (database unverifiable due to persistent credential failure; constructed strictly from documented schemas and precedents):\n\n",
      "tool_calls": [
        {
          "id": "call_05c27082b4b248dfb42fc48e",
          "type": "function",
          "function": {
            "name": "submit_SQL",
            "arguments": "{\"sql\": \"WITH dept_enrollment_stats AS (\\n    SELECT sd.DEPARTMENT_NAME,\\n           AVG(tso.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) AS avg_enrollment,\\n           VARIANCE(tso.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) AS enrollment_variance\\n    FROM TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED tso\\n    JOIN SIS_DEPARTMENT sd ON tso.OFFER_DEPT_CODE = sd.DEPARTMENT_CODE\\n    JOIN SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION scd ON sd.DEPARTMENT_CODE = scd.DEPARTMENT\\n    WHERE tso.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS > 0\\n      AND scd.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y'\\n      AND sd.DEPARTMENT_CODE <> '17'\\n    GROUP BY sd.DEPARTMENT_NAME, sd.DEPARTMENT_CODE\\n),\\nchem_bio_year_stats AS (\\n    SELECT ata.ACADEMIC_YEAR,\\n           COUNT(tso.SUBJECT_ID) AS subject_count,\\n           MIN(ata.TERM_START_DATE) AS min_term_start_date\\n    FROM TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED tso\\n    JOIN ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL ata ON tso.TERM_CODE = ata.TERM_CODE\\n    JOIN ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER atp ON ata.TERM_CODE = atp.TERM_CODE\\n    WHERE tso.OFFER_DEPT_NAME IN ('Chemistry', 'Biology')\\n      AND tso.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS > 0\\n    GROUP BY ata.ACADEMIC_YEAR\\n)\\nSELECT d.DEPARTMENT_NAME,\\n       d.avg_enrollment,\\n       d.enrollment_variance,\\n       c.ACADEMIC_YEAR,\\n       c.subject_count,\\n       c.min_term_start_date\\nFROM dept_enrollment_stats d\\nCROSS JOIN chem_bio_year_stats c\\nORDER BY d.DEPARTMENT_NAME, c.ACADEMIC_YEAR\"}"
          }
